&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top 2 Comments:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NewsaHackO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;I get using LLMs to help proofread or copywrite a blog post, but whats the point of just regurgitating a ChatGPT answer in a blog post and posting it here? If it&amp;#x27;s really that interesting, couldn&amp;#x27;t you just post the prompt so that we can see it for ourselves?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div style="margin: 10px 0; padding: 10px; background: #f6f6f6; border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;"&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0 0 5px 0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;nasretdinov:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin: 0;"&gt;Nice article! One nitpick: Go can build C code via cgo when doing go get, but of course that probably won&amp;#x27;t generate the object files Ruby modules are expecting.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
